  "_precision": "Numbers the paper prints with a fixed number of decimals are stored as STRINGS holding the printed literal (thousands separators dropped so float() parses them), because JSON numbers cannot carry trailing zeros: 0.40 would read back as 0.4 and compare() would then apply tolerance 0.05 instead of 0.005. notebooks/_common.py compare() takes the decimal count from the string. Values the paper prints in scientific notation (table19_qm9.lr '2x10^-3', table20_qm9.peak_lr '10^-6') stay numeric; the notebook passes decimals= for those."
